    },
    "Check that Ferry is on under File Providers in Login Items & Extensions." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Checking…" : {

    },
    "Choose **Refresh** in the Ferry menu." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Choose Developer Tools, then Device Info…, to see the model, Android version, build, serial number, battery, IP addresses and storage the device reports. Ferry only reads them. Copy puts them on the clipboard." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Choose Developer Tools, then Logcat…, to watch the device's log in a window of its own. Ferry keeps the newest 50,000 lines. Level shows lines at that level and above, and Filter shows the lines that contain your text, whatever its case. Pause freezes the window while lines keep arriving, and Resume catches up. Clear empties it." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Choose Developer Tools, then Open Shell, to open Terminal with a shell on the device (adb shell). Ferry needs adb for this, and says so if it can't find it. Nothing on the device changes unless you type a command that changes it." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Choose Developer Tools, then Port Forwarding…, to send connections to a port on this Mac to a port on the device. Type the port on this Mac (1024 or higher) and the port on the device, then click Add. Remove ends a forward." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
