    "Ferry Help" : {

    },
    "Ferry can't save to your screenshot folder or the Desktop. Allow Ferry in Privacy & Security." : {

    },
    "Ferry has no address for this device. Connect it by address." : {

    },
    "Ferry has no telemetry, no analytics and no account, and sends nothing to any server. Your files go only between the device and your Mac. If you use ADB over Wi-Fi, Ferry talks to that device on your network and nowhere else." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Ferry is waiting for its helper to answer, for example just after Ferry opens." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Ferry knows this device at another address. Confirm the new one in the menu." : {

    },
    "Ferry needs adb, from Google's Android platform tools. If it is missing, the menu shows **Install adb for more tools…** and the command to run: `brew install --cask android-platform-tools`. Click **Check again** once it is installed." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Ferry reaches the device over ADB on a USB cable." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Ferry reaches the device over ADB on your network." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Ferry reaches the device over USB file transfer. Turn on USB debugging to use ADB instead." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Ferry saves them where macOS saves its own screenshots (the Desktop, unless you chose another folder in the Screenshot app), named like macOS's own, such as Screenshot LinkRunner-100G 2026-11-18 at 17.09.27.png, and shows them in Finder. It never replaces a file. A recording waits on the device until Ferry has saved it, even if you quit Ferry meanwhile; Ferry then removes it from the device." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Ferry shows Android devices as locations in Finder. It runs in the menu bar and has no Dock icon." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Ferry switches to ADB as soon as you allow this Mac on the device." : {

    },
    "Ferry's help could not be loaded. Reinstalling Ferry restores it." : {

    },
    "Ferry's helper is not responding" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Ferry's helper is not responding. Quit Ferry and open it again." : {

    },
    "Ferry's locations are all off in System Settings. Click **Open System Settings** and turn on Ferry under File Providers. Shown once a device has been connected." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "File transfer" : {

    },
    "File transfer is off or the device is locked. Choose **Transfer files** on the device, then **Refresh**." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Files copied from a device, and folders on it named like an app or a document package, are marked as downloaded, so macOS checks an app or script with Gatekeeper before it first opens, as it does for one from the internet." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Files over 4 GB copy to internal storage. Many SD cards cannot hold a file over 4 GB; Ferry shows an error instead of copying part of it." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
